ity of the  accounts and supporting working papers  last year and a reduced number of  differences identified i think this year  that positive direction of travel has  continued  we've only actually reported one audit  difference in our audit results report  which is a very  small difference which i will highlight  to you in more detail  so i really just wanted to take the  opportunity to say that particularly in  the difficult circumstances that we've  all been facing since march  um i think the process for the  production of the accounts and the  process to support our audit  um has been excellent and so and thank  you very much to the finance team for  all their support through that  as noah has said we have substantially  completed the audit and i will take you  through the areas that have still got to  be complete which are very much  administrative in nature  um and i'll just explain a little bit  more detail what they are and therefore  why we're not in a position to actually  sign off the accounts um  at this date if i can take members to  the executive summary which starts on  page  6.9 of your numbering  i wanted to highlight here to you some  of the changes  that we've had to make to our audit  strategy and following the issue of our  audit plan  back in july the main changes as you  would expect have been as a result of  ovid 19.  naomi's already highlighted the changes  to the reporting timetable  so i won't recap on that but then we've  also considered where kobit 19 could  have an impact on the financial  statements  and that's primarily in relation to  balance sheet items and also disclosures  within the accounts  and we've highlighted there two of the  initial ones that we identified which  was  the potential to um the council to  revisit the way it calculates the bad  debt provision because of the  possible greater default of people on  debts as a result again of the  impact on the economy from kobe 19.  we've also flagged the need for enhanced  di